# PDFs are binary, even when they look like text.
#
# The hand-built fixtures under tests/ and benchmarks/ are minimal PDFs made almost
# entirely of ASCII, so Git heuristics classify them as text. On a clone with
# core.autocrlf=true every LF inside them becomes CRLF, the byte offsets in the xref
# table stop matching, and pypdf can no longer open the file -- surfacing as a test
# failure that points nowhere near the real cause.
*.pdf binary
